(5913054, 862112, 43774, '<td valign="top">Very good, great detail and clarity. It took me a while to figure out what it was sitting on though. Maybe the backgorund of stones is a bit too much?</td>', 'Very good, great detail and clarity. It took me a while to figure out what it was sitting on though. Maybe the backgorund of stones is a bit too much?', '2010-03-22 09:46:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5913059, 862167, 104841, '<td valign="top">I like the location and the way you have lit the scene. To my eyes the shady side of the car appears to have a slight blue tinge (did you get the WB 100%?) and the halo around the trees does not look good a tall. This can happen if you use some HDR packages. If you did not use such a package you need to get in tighter with the brush to darken the sky. There are also some specks/bids that you might want to consider removing.</td>', 'I like the location and the way you have lit the scene. To my eyes the shady side of the car appears to have a slight blue tinge (did you get the WB 100%?) and the halo around the trees does not look good a tall. This can happen if you use some HDR packages. If you did not use such a package you need to get in tighter with the brush to darken the sky. There are also some specks/bids that you might want to consider removing.', '2010-03-22 09:50:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5913068, 861724, 104841, '<td valign="top">nice product placement with planet of room for text for the advert. I think that the snow is just about right maybe a tad too bright. There does appears to be some white spots appears in the shot. I don''t know if they are falling snow or dust on the lens but I would have cloned them out.</td>', 'nice product placement with planet of room for text for the advert. I think that the snow is just about right maybe a tad too bright. There does appears to be some white spots appears in the shot. I don''t know if they are falling snow or dust on the lens but I would have cloned them out.', '2010-03-22 09:55:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5913071, 861082, 44825, '<td valign="top">Good shot but as a product shot this is a bit confusing - Is it Canon or Sigma?</td>', 'Good shot but as a product shot this is a bit confusing - Is it Canon or Sigma?', '2010-03-22 09:57:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5913082, 860959, 86447, '<td valign="top">Cool!  I''d have cropped the top part so that pink flower doesn''t clash with the gorgeous red of Coca-Cola.  Well done, though!   (Not voting)</td>', 'Cool!  I''d have cropped the top part so that pink flower doesn''t clash with the gorgeous red of Coca-Cola.  Well done, though!   (Not voting)', '2010-03-22 10:19:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5913083, 861724, 30982, '<td valign="top">Bold and different product shot - would work well in a catalog, I think.  (Commenting only.)</td>', 'Bold and different product shot - would work well in a catalog, I think.  (Commenting only.)', '2010-03-22 10:21:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(5913085, 862131, 30982, '<td valign="top">I didn''t know they still made this.  I think my Dad wore this when I was a kid!  Excellent photograph - would work very well as a real ad.  (Commenting only.)</td>', 'I didn''t know they still made this.  I think my Dad wore this when I was a kid!  Excellent photograph - would work very well as a real ad.  (Commenting only.)', '2010-03-22 10:22:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5913086, 861653, 30982, '<td valign="top">The product is displayed well in an uncluttered space and the lighting is OK, but it needs a bit something more, though I would be hardpressed to tell you what that is.  (Commenting only.)</td>', 'The product is displayed well in an uncluttered space and the lighting is OK, but it needs a bit something more, though I would be hardpressed to tell you what that is.  (Commenting only.)', '2010-03-22 10:23:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5913087, 862099, 86447, '<td valign="top">LOVELY JOB!   I can almost reach out and feel them, they''re so well photographed!   <br/> <br/>My only nitpick is that I think there needs to be at least a small bit of shadow at the base of the box.  It appears to be floating.  (Not voting)</td>', 'LOVELY JOB!   I can almost reach out and feel them, they''re so well photographed!    My only nitpick is that I think there needs to be at least a small bit of shadow at the base of the box.  It appears to be floating.  (Not voting)', '2010-03-22 10:24:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5913089, 862180, 30982, '<td valign="top">Excellent title for the ad!  And gotta love this stuff.  For a true product shoot, I''m guessing you''d want to eliminate the reflections on the can, particularly where they run across the product name.  Great approach, though!  (Commenting only.)</td>', 'Excellent title for the ad!  And gotta love this stuff.  For a true product shoot, I''m guessing you''d want to eliminate the reflections on the can, particularly where they run across the product name.  Great approach, though!  (Commenting only.)', '2010-03-22 10:24:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(5913090, 861937, 30982, '<td valign="top">A good look at the product "in use" so to speak (as in mounted on the bike).  You could crop the top off as it serves no purpose for the product shot per se.  And though it might be tough with a real bike, you''d probably want that foreground cable out of the way for the catalog shot.  (Commenting only.)</td>', 'A good look at the product "in use" so to speak (as in mounted on the bike).  You could crop the top off as it serves no purpose for the product shot per se.  And though it might be tough with a real bike, you''d probably want that foreground cable out of the way for the catalog shot.  (Commenting only.)', '2010-03-22 10:25:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(5913092, 862186, 30982, '<td valign="top">I like the shallow DPF in this, but am not sure about the horizontal presentation.  Also, if you look through catalogs and magazines, you''ll find that analog watches are almost always set to 10 past 2.  For some odd reason, ad men in the 40s determined that was the most aesthetically pleasing view of a watch face.  (Commenting only.)</td>', 'I like the shallow DPF in this, but am not sure about the horizontal presentation.  Also, if you look through catalogs and magazines, you''ll find that analog watches are almost always set to 10 past 2.  For some odd reason, ad men in the 40s determined that was the most aesthetically pleasing view of a watch face.  (Commenting only.)', '2010-03-22 10:27:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5913095, 862122, 30982, '<td valign="top">Good job of making your product front and center but you need to have that focus be dead on for an add - you''d have to use a bit more DOF if possible to keep it all in perfect focus.  I''m not sure your background helps you here - the colors are good but the pattern takes away a bit from the product itself.  Light is even and natural!  (Commenting only.)</td>', 'Good job of making your product front and center but you need to have that focus be dead on for an add - you''d have to use a bit more DOF if possible to keep it all in perfect focus.  I''m not sure your background helps you here - the colors are good but the pattern takes away a bit from the product itself.  Light is even and natural!  (Commenting only.)', '2010-03-22 10:28:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5913098, 862144, 86447, '<td valign="top">LOVELY abstract! One of my faves of all time, I think. ( You folks are funny!)  (not voting)</td>', 'LOVELY abstract! One of my faves of all time, I think. ( You folks are funny!)  (not voting)', '2010-03-22 10:29:56.000000', NULL, 1),
