(5923205, 861933, 12448, '<td valign="top">I saw that trademark as well and wondered why it was disqualified.  Was it added after the fact by DPC and if so, why not on all of the entries?</td>', 'I saw that trademark as well and wondered why it was disqualified.  Was it added after the fact by DPC and if so, why not on all of the entries?', '2010-03-31 07:54:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5923637, 861933, 113634, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DAWAR:</b></div><hr/><i> Embedded Copy right Kelmark 10 in the picture of a member seems....?<br/>Will you comment about it to make it authentic ?<br/>Criticism from other members  ? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>did i do something wrong by adding a watermark to my photo?  i just thought i was protecting my image from being stolen.... i''ve had so many views on my profile since this ribbon, i thought i needed to protect myself (and my pics).  if i used this incorrectly or in bad taste, that was not my intention at all..... my only intent was protect my photos</td>', 'Originally posted by DAWAR: Embedded Copy right Kelmark 10 in the picture of a member seems....?Will you comment about it to make it authentic ?Criticism from other members  ?   did i do something wrong by adding a watermark to my photo?  i just thought i was protecting my image from being stolen.... i''ve had so many views on my profile since this ribbon, i thought i needed to protect myself (and my pics).  if i used this incorrectly or in bad taste, that was not my intention at all..... my only intent was protect my photos', '2010-03-31 14:25:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5924172, 861933, 49916, '<td valign="top">Yes my friend, it is authentic as per rules newly created. The size of the image on DPC are not high resolution. They can not be used for professional purpose. They give just an idea to the budding photographer about the techniques used and not more than that. I wanted to make this picture my favorite, but I felt the copy right text like an ugly spot on a beautiful face. I perhaps may be wrong !<br/>Anyway, it is a very creative idea,hard labor and excellent result.Keep it up in future !<br/>Many many congrats for a BLUE :-)</td>', 'Yes my friend, it is authentic as per rules newly created. The size of the image on DPC are not high resolution. They can not be used for professional purpose. They give just an idea to the budding photographer about the techniques used and not more than that. I wanted to make this picture my favorite, but I felt the copy right text like an ugly spot on a beautiful face. I perhaps may be wrong !Anyway, it is a very creative idea,hard labor and excellent result.Keep it up in future !Many many congrats for a BLUE :-)', '2010-03-31 22:56:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5924265, 861544, 66515, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club!<br/> <br/>First of all, thank you so much for including your lighting setup. It really helps us understand what you were trying to do when we do our critiques for these types of images and helps other learn as well.<br/> <br/>In terms of the lighting it does look a little too bright in the top left and on the upper left edge of the bowl. It almost looks like that light (the soft box if I am reading your setup correctly) was a bit brighter than the light with the snoot. I''d be curious to see what this looks like shot without the softbox.  Otherwise, the lighting is pretty good. <br/> <br/>The focus for this image might be a little soft. Or at the very least there might not be enough DOF. (I think that might be it)  Composition is ok and you have your elements positioned in a pleasing way. Maybe getting a little lower would add more emphasis to the brand name on the bowl. Then again getting lower would necessitate increasing your DOF even more I think.<br/> <br/>For the challenge? Terrific choice of subject.  The textures and the colors you presented really sold the viewers and made them want to be person getting that chocolate covered strawberry out of the bowl. At the end of the day, in my opinion, that was the most important goal and you suceeded at it.  <br/> <br/>Congratulations on your personal best and I hope you didn''t get too full "cleaning up your set". :)</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club! First of all, thank you so much for including your lighting setup. It really helps us understand what you were trying to do when we do our critiques for these types of images and helps other learn as well. In terms of the lighting it does look a little too bright in the top left and on the upper left edge of the bowl. It almost looks like that light (the soft box if I am reading your setup correctly) was a bit brighter than the light with the snoot. I''d be curious to see what this looks like shot without the softbox.  Otherwise, the lighting is pretty good.  The focus for this image might be a little soft. Or at the very least there might not be enough DOF. (I think that might be it)  Composition is ok and you have your elements positioned in a pleasing way. Maybe getting a little lower would add more emphasis to the brand name on the bowl. Then again getting lower would necessitate increasing your DOF even more I think. For the challenge? Terrific choice of subject.  The textures and the colors you presented really sold the viewers and made them want to be person getting that chocolate covered strawberry out of the bowl. At the end of the day, in my opinion, that was the most important goal and you suceeded at it.   Congratulations on your personal best and I hope you didn''t get too full "cleaning up your set". :)', '2010-04-01 00:00:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5924664, 861933, 63633, '<td valign="top">There''s nothing wrong with adding the watermark Kelly. That''s exactly what the feature is there for. There have been plenty of examples of "low-res" files being ripped off for commercial purposes, including one by <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=40718" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">DrAchoo</a> that was used for a billboard!</td>', 'There''s nothing wrong with adding the watermark Kelly. That''s exactly what the feature is there for. There have been plenty of examples of "low-res" files being ripped off for commercial purposes, including one by  DrAchoo that was used for a billboard!', '2010-04-01 02:48:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5924674, 862187, 106543, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club! </b> <br/> <br/>Ughh I had a bunch of stuff written and lost it because my computer froze. Second time around will hopefully be better and make more sense. While it doesn''t really meet the challenge, as I''m sure you''re aware of, it''s still a very interesting picture. Particularly that orange stripe. I voted this a 6. I''m not really sure why, there is no product involved. Just something about this picture that I liked. Page 13 of the abstract catalogue was selling inner peace it seems.<br/> <br/>I really hope you don''t leave DPC Don, I love that thread you have and your images always show me things I wouldn''t think to photograph. What will Team Suck do without it''s leader?<br/> <br/>If you have any questions <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=106543" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">click here to message me</a>! <br/> <br/>Senay</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!   Ughh I had a bunch of stuff written and lost it because my computer froze. Second time around will hopefully be better and make more sense. While it doesn''t really meet the challenge, as I''m sure you''re aware of, it''s still a very interesting picture. Particularly that orange stripe. I voted this a 6. I''m not really sure why, there is no product involved. Just something about this picture that I liked. Page 13 of the abstract catalogue was selling inner peace it seems. I really hope you don''t leave DPC Don, I love that thread you have and your images always show me things I wouldn''t think to photograph. What will Team Suck do without it''s leader? If you have any questions click here to message me!  Senay', '2010-04-01 03:11:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5924685, 861738, 106543, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!  </b> <br/> <br/>This was one of my favourites of the challenge. Also I noticed Carlsberg fairly quickly, I love that stuff haha.  This would look perfectly natural as an ad in a magazine. Centering the watch was perfect, title works amazingly well with how you set this up.<br/> <br/>At first I agreed with the commenter who suggested a square crop, but thinking of this appearing in a magazine the crop would have to be more like this so it works better this way. I guess it all just depends on how you see it being advertised.<br/> <br/>I think I like this one better than your outtake but if you had the colours/contrast of that one in this picture it might have given you a higher score. Overall great work! And you''re only 16 so even more awesome! I hope I get to see more of your work show up.<br/> <br/>If you have any questions <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=106543" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">click here to message me</a>! <br/> <br/>Senay</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!    This was one of my favourites of the challenge. Also I noticed Carlsberg fairly quickly, I love that stuff haha.  This would look perfectly natural as an ad in a magazine. Centering the watch was perfect, title works amazingly well with how you set this up. At first I agreed with the commenter who suggested a square crop, but thinking of this appearing in a magazine the crop would have to be more like this so it works better this way. I guess it all just depends on how you see it being advertised. I think I like this one better than your outtake but if you had the colours/contrast of that one in this picture it might have given you a higher score. Overall great work! And you''re only 16 so even more awesome! I hope I get to see more of your work show up. If you have any questions click here to message me!  Senay', '2010-04-01 03:32:26.000000', NULL, 0),
