(5925879, 861933, 106543, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club! </b> <br/> <br/>Why did I end up with your picture!? It was one of my highest rated pictures in the challenge and you won the blue, I''m definitely not worthy! Congratulations by the way and I hope everything worked out with the validation!<br/> <br/>This is such a creative picture, I wish I had these kind of ideas. 7.7 score is just amazing, that''ll be one hard personal best to beat. Reading through the comments there were a couple things that people picked up that I didn''t notice. The tiny bit of black in the very bottom right, the yellow corn on the S and people wanted a whiter background. Those are the only very small things that could be fixed in this picture.<br/> <br/>Looking at the votes you got, you only received 6 votes under a 6. Has that ever happened before? Excellent job and hop to see more great entries from you.<br/> <br/>If you have any questions <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=106543" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">click here to message me</a>! <br/> <br/>Senay <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!   Why did I end up with your picture!? It was one of my highest rated pictures in the challenge and you won the blue, I''m definitely not worthy! Congratulations by the way and I hope everything worked out with the validation! This is such a creative picture, I wish I had these kind of ideas. 7.7 score is just amazing, that''ll be one hard personal best to beat. Reading through the comments there were a couple things that people picked up that I didn''t notice. The tiny bit of black in the very bottom right, the yellow corn on the S and people wanted a whiter background. Those are the only very small things that could be fixed in this picture. Looking at the votes you got, you only received 6 votes under a 6. Has that ever happened before? Excellent job and hop to see more great entries from you. If you have any questions click here to message me!  Senay ', '2010-04-01 16:35:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5926947, 861946, 106543, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club! </b> <br/> <br/>This was one of my highest rated pictures in the Product Shot challenge. I gave you a 9.<br/> <br/>This stuff is delicious first of all so I was biased in your favour hehe. Personally I really liked the dark lighting. The tea matches perfectly with the bottle. There''s not much I would change about this. You received some helpful comments though. And I have to agree that it would have been nice to have the edge of the cap lighted as well. I''m surprised this didn''t score higher though.<br/> <br/>Josh you keep replacing your top rated images on your profile, keep up the great work! Love your stuff!<br/> <br/>If you have any questions <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=106543" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">click here to message me</a>! <br/> <br/>Senay</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!   This was one of my highest rated pictures in the Product Shot challenge. I gave you a 9. This stuff is delicious first of all so I was biased in your favour hehe. Personally I really liked the dark lighting. The tea matches perfectly with the bottle. There''s not much I would change about this. You received some helpful comments though. And I have to agree that it would have been nice to have the edge of the cap lighted as well. I''m surprised this didn''t score higher though. Josh you keep replacing your top rated images on your profile, keep up the great work! Love your stuff! If you have any questions click here to message me!  Senay', '2010-04-02 02:31:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5926957, 862049, 106543, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club! </b> <br/> <br/>How is this fair? I just critiqued the blue ribbon for this contest earlier. I hardly feel like I''m qualified to critique your picture, but I''ll give it a shot. :)<br/> <br/>I''ll start off with the negatives. There are none haha. Hmmm if there was one thing I''d change though it would be to have the reflection of the watch face showing instead of shining so much light. Actually your way works good to isolate the watch face from the reflection so as to draw the focus to it.<br/> <br/>I like the DOF, the water droplets look great in focus and in the back too. I hope you weren''t expecting an extremely helpful critique, there''s really nothing to improve . You placed third and have a new personal best, congratulations!<br/> <br/>If you have any questions <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=106543" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">click here to message me</a>! <br/> <br/>Senay</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!   How is this fair? I just critiqued the blue ribbon for this contest earlier. I hardly feel like I''m qualified to critique your picture, but I''ll give it a shot. :) I''ll start off with the negatives. There are none haha. Hmmm if there was one thing I''d change though it would be to have the reflection of the watch face showing instead of shining so much light. Actually your way works good to isolate the watch face from the reflection so as to draw the focus to it. I like the DOF, the water droplets look great in focus and in the back too. I hope you weren''t expecting an extremely helpful critique, there''s really nothing to improve . You placed third and have a new personal best, congratulations! If you have any questions click here to message me!  Senay', '2010-04-02 02:47:59.000000', NULL, 0),
