(5927267, 861933, 30982, '<td valign="top">Oh dear, that''s really too bad.  But yes, viewing software (like Windows Viewer) for instance, does indeed change the data if you rotate a file.  NEVER do anything to your originals.  If need be, make two folders and put the shots in each folder, mark one as "Original", the other as "Working".  Then if you don''t need the original you can dump that folder later.  Make sense?  <br/> <br/>Still a darn fine shot and I still think you should send it to the company!</td>', 'Oh dear, that''s really too bad.  But yes, viewing software (like Windows Viewer) for instance, does indeed change the data if you rotate a file.  NEVER do anything to your originals.  If need be, make two folders and put the shots in each folder, mark one as "Original", the other as "Working".  Then if you don''t need the original you can dump that folder later.  Make sense?   Still a darn fine shot and I still think you should send it to the company!', '2010-04-02 11:31:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5927273, 862099, 9114, '<td valign="top">Are the chocolates gone now? LOL<br/>Nice shot<br/>Debbi</td>', 'Are the chocolates gone now? LOLNice shotDebbi', '2010-04-02 11:35:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5927333, 861933, 37845, '<td valign="top">This is tragic... Sorry about the DQ. But, as many people say, blue ribbon or not, it is an amazing image. <br/> <br/>I had a close call with the same issue you had. Rotated an image in windows, and it modified the image. Now, I shoot everything in RAW. The RAW image serves well as the original. Hope your camera shoots in RAW. <br/> <br/></td>', 'This is tragic... Sorry about the DQ. But, as many people say, blue ribbon or not, it is an amazing image.  I had a close call with the same issue you had. Rotated an image in windows, and it modified the image. Now, I shoot everything in RAW. The RAW image serves well as the original. Hope your camera shoots in RAW.  ', '2010-04-02 12:09:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5927353, 861933, 28359, '<td valign="top">Great image, took a lot of work to get it right. Sorry about the DQ. Still a Great job!</td>', 'Great image, took a lot of work to get it right. Sorry about the DQ. Still a Great job!', '2010-04-02 12:29:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5927377, 861933, 74911, '<td valign="top">Sorry about the DQ, Kelly. I had a DQ for almost the same reason. From then on, I shoot RAW and submit the RAW file for validation. With JPEG, there is always a chance that it might get rotated and saved, if we are not careful with the message that pops up. I learnt it a hard way and I know exactly how it feels.<br/> <br/>Raj</td>', 'Sorry about the DQ, Kelly. I had a DQ for almost the same reason. From then on, I shoot RAW and submit the RAW file for validation. With JPEG, there is always a chance that it might get rotated and saved, if we are not careful with the message that pops up. I learnt it a hard way and I know exactly how it feels. Raj', '2010-04-02 12:48:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5927386, 861720, 28359, '<td valign="top">The King of product shots gets his Blue :-). Nice work!!!, (no manner what color the ribbon is)..Lol</td>', 'The King of product shots gets his Blue :-). Nice work!!!, (no manner what color the ribbon is)..Lol', '2010-04-02 12:56:59.000000', NULL, 0),
